course: dictionary
lesson: 15258
title: Strong speaking verbs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shriek means to give a sudden, very high, loud cry. «Shrieked» is the past form, so it tells us this happened before now. The children shrieked, so they were making a sudden, very high, loud sound.
explain: Writers choose «shrieked» instead of «said» or «shouted» because it tells the reader how a character feels. «Mum shrieked in terror when she saw the mouse» shows she was frightened. «Mum said, "Look at that mouse"» tells us nothing about her feelings.
explain: Shriek can also describe things, not just people. «The brakes shrieked as the bus stopped» means the brakes made a high, sharp, screeching noise. Try your meaning in the sentence: does a high, sharp noise fit? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Shriek means to give a sudden, very high, loud cry.
fact: «Shrieked» is the past form of «shriek».
fact: «Shrieked» can mean a cry of fear, pain, excitement or laughter.
fact: «Shrieked with laughter» means laughing in a high, loud way.
fact: Things can shriek too, such as brakes, wind or a whistle, when they make a high, sharp noise.
exercise: «The little boy shrieked with laughter.» What does shrieked mean here? | Whispered quietly to his friend | Ran out of the room | Fell fast asleep | *Gave a sudden, high, loud cry of laughter
exercise: «The brakes shrieked as the car stopped.» What made the shrieking sound? | The driver | The road | *The brakes | The rain
exercise: «She shrieked in terror when she saw the spider.» Which word could replace shrieked and keep the meaning close? | *screamed | whispered | yawned | smiled
test: «Mum shrieked in terror when she saw the mouse.» Why is «shrieked» a better word than «said» here? | It shows she was very quiet | It shows she was bored and tired | It shows she was sleeping | *It shows she was frightened and her voice was loud
test: «The seagulls shrieked over the harbour.» What were the seagulls doing? | Swimming quietly under the water | *Making loud, sharp cries | Sleeping on the boats | Singing a soft lullaby
exam: «The children shrieked with excitement as the bell rang for the holidays.» What does shrieked show about the children? | They were hiding under their desks | They were tired and bored | They were cross with the teacher | *They were wildly excited and loud
